title: Start
---
== start
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
A colorful merchant caravan is stopped by the roadside, its canvas covers fluttering in the breeze. The merchant, a portly man with a waxed mustache and fine velvet clothes, calls out to you.

"Ho there, soldier! Fine goods for sale! I have everything a fighting man might need - rations, wine, even a few luxury items from Paris!"

<<setCharacter merchant>>
<<advanceTime 15>>
What do you do?
* "[Browse his wares]"
    <<jump browse_goods>>
* "[What news from the south?]"
    <<jump ask_news>>
* "[Move along, I'm on duty.]"
    <<move_on>>
* "[Your papers, merchant.]"
    <<jump check_papers>>

== browse_goods
<<showImage artwork/merchant_goods.jpg>>
The merchant rubs his hands together eagerly. "Excellent! I have:

- Salted beef: 5 coins each (lasts for weeks!)
- Fine wine: 8 coins per bottle (much better than army swill!)
- Leather gloves: 12 coins (protect your hands from sword calluses)
- Silver crucifix: 25 coins (for protection, of course!)
- French perfume: 30 coins (impress the ladies, eh?)"

<<setCharacter merchant>>
<<advanceTime 30>>
What interests you?
* Buy salted beef (5 coins)
    <<if hasItem coins, 5>>
        <<removeItem coins, 5>>
        <<addItem salted_beef, 1>>
        <<addFlag merchant_customer, 1>>
        "A wise choice!" The merchant hands you a wrapped package. "This will keep you strong when army rations run low!"
        <<jump finish_browsing>>
    <<else>>
        You check your coin pouch - not enough money.
        <<jump browse_goods>>
    <<endif>>
* Buy fine wine (8 coins)
    <<if hasItem coins, 8>>
        <<removeItem coins, 8>>
        <<addItem fine_wine, 1>>
        <<addFlag merchant_customer, 1>>
        "Ah, a man of taste!" The merchant winks. "This will make those long nights in camp much more pleasant."
        <<jump finish_browsing>>
    <<else>>
        You check your coin pouch - not enough money.
        <<jump browse_goods>>
    <<endif>>
* Buy leather gloves (12 coins)
    <<if hasItem coins, 12>>
        <<removeItem coins, 12>>
        <<addItem leather_gloves, 1>>
        <<addFlag merchant_customer, 1>>
        "Quality craftsmanship!" The merchant holds up the gloves. "Your hands will thank you after a long day with your sword."
        <<jump finish_browsing>>
    <<else>>
        You check your coin pouch - not enough money.
        <<jump browse_goods>>
    <<endif>>
* "Nothing interests me."
    <<jump finish_browsing>>

== finish_browsing
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant bows deeply. "A pleasure doing business with you! Safe travels, soldier!"

<<if hasFlag merchant_customer>>
    <<addFlag merchant_friend, 1>>
    "Come back anytime! I travel this road regularly."
<<endif>>

* Continue on your way
    <<stop>>

== ask_news
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant leans in conspiratorially. "News? I have plenty!

The French are massing troops near Orleans - big trouble coming. English commanders are arguing about strategy again. And I heard the King himself may be coming to inspect the troops soon!"

<<advanceTime 20>>
What do you ask?
* "Tell me more about the French troops"
    <<jump french_troops_news>>
* "What about the King's visit?"
    <<jump king_visit_news>>
* "Any news about supply lines?"
    <<jump supply_news>>

== french_troops_news
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
"Rumors of heavy cavalry, maybe even some of those Scottish mercenaries they love so much. Farmers are fleeing the area. If I were you, I'd be careful traveling south of the Loire."

<<addFlag knows_french_threat, 1>>
* "Good to know. Anything else?"
    <<jump ask_news>>
* "I should be going."
    <<stop>>

== king_visit_news
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
"Supposed to be next month! Everyone's scrambling to clean up the camps and make things look proper. I hear there might be promotions for soldiers who impress him."

<<addFlag knows_king_visit, 1>>
* "Interesting. What else do you know?"
    <<jump ask_news>>
* "Thank you for the information."
    <<stop>>

== supply_news
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant sighs. "Troubling news. The main supply convoy was attacked by bandits last week. Army's running short on everything - especially arrows and salt. That's why my prices are so high, you understand!"

<<addFlag knows_supply_shortage, 1>>
* "I see. Any other news?"
    <<jump ask_news>>
* "I should get moving."
    <<stop>>

== check_papers
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant pales and fumbles in his satchel. "Papers? Of course, of course! I have all the proper permits from the Sheriff of Kent..."

He produces a slightly damp document with an official-looking seal. Everything appears to be in order.

<<advanceTime 15>>
What do you do?
* "Everything seems fine. Carry on."
    <<jump let_pass>>
* "This seal looks suspicious."
    <<jump suspicious_seal>>

== let_pass
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant wipes sweat from his brow. "Thank you, sir! Much appreciated! Here, take this for your trouble."

He presses a small coin into your hand before quickly packing up and moving on.

<<addItem coins, 2>>
<<addFlag merchant_bribe, 1>>
* Continue patrol
    <<stop>>

== suspicious_seal
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant's eyes widen in panic. "Suspicious? No, no! It's perfectly legitimate! I paid good money for that seal!"

He's sweating profusely and won't meet your eyes.

<<advanceTime 20>>
What do you do?
* "I'm confiscating these goods until we verify the papers."
    <<jump confiscate_goods>>
* "Get out of my sight before I change my mind."
    <<jump let_pass_angry>>

== confiscate_goods
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant looks devastated. "Please, sir! That's my entire livelihood! I have a family to feed!"

<<advanceTime 30>>
What do you do?
* "I can't help you. The goods stay here."
    <<jump harsh_confiscation>>
* "Fine. Take your papers and go, but leave the goods."
    <<jump merciful_confiscation>>

== harsh_confiscation
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant weeps openly as you begin unloading his cart. "You're ruining me! God have mercy on your soul!"

You find several valuable items among his goods.

<<addItem fine_wine, 2>>
<<addItem silver_crucifix, 1>>
<<addFlag harsh_confiscator, 1>>
<<addFlag merchant_ruined, 1>>
* Leave with the confiscated goods
    <<stop>>

== merciful_confiscation
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
"Thank you, sir! Thank you!" The merchant bows repeatedly. "I won't forget your mercy!"

He quickly packs up and flees, leaving behind a small token of his gratitude.

<<addItem leather_gloves, 1>>
<<addFlag merciful_soldier, 1>>
* Let him go
    <<stop>>

== let_pass_angry
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant scrambles to pack up, nearly dropping several packages in his haste. "Yes, sir! Right away, sir!"

He's gone in a cloud of dust, leaving behind a small pouch that fell from his belt.

<<addItem coins, 5>>
<<addFlag merchant_intimidated, 1>>
* Take the coins and continue
    <<stop>>

== move_on
<<showImage artwork/merchant_caravan.jpg>>
The merchant shrugs. "Your loss, soldier! Fine goods for fine prices!"

He calls out to the next soldiers passing by.

<<addFlag merchant_ignored, 1>>
* Continue on your way
    <<stop>>
===
